  "contract": [
    "Reuse the existing GAP profile owner at0x200064c0. Shrink the old observer flags from3 to2 bytes at0x200064be..bf; observer ff-to1 repair and both parameter-selection reads use the canonical profile.",
    "Reuse the existing two preferred parameter records at0x99182 and0x9918a. Add only the slow record72/84/4/600 and glasses record16/16/2/600, matching the other two stock records.",
    "Handleffff is a no-effect path. Matching phone flags skip before mode selection; matching glasses handle with flag1 skips mode2. Other modes select slow; mode1 selects by live profile; mode2 uses the glasses record.",
    "The SDK owns SVC7a preferred-parameter setup and SVC75 connection update. Mode1 tolerates setup busy17; modes0/other and2 log it. Setupffff is logged then aborts. Mode1/2 tolerate update busy17; slow updates log every nonzero status. Error logging can return.",
    "The fast byte is written only after setup continuation, before the connection update. Mode1 reloads the profile after setup/error callbacks, even though the two records currently have equal bytes.",
    "The slow wrappers cancel the existing delayed callback with connection<<16, then schedule the same argument at0 or0x2800 depending on any nonzero immediate word; the again wrapper uses0x2c00. These are raw delay units.",
    "The flag getter returns one byte at0x200064f8; the adjacent setter stores the low byte and preserves its full uint32 return word."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This supplies hardware connection-control leaves. The BLE queue consumer at0x45184 remains an explicit import; no complete queued consumer or link-security lifecycle is claimed.",
    "The native SDK gateway instructions and real C handle getters, observer, GAP checked setter and delayed event callback execute in the probe. Supervisor service results, log sinks, role query, schedule/cancel backend and queue encoder are prepared models. There is no radio, scheduler or flash operation.",
    "The Nordic uint16 connection key is compared at SVC75. Native incidental upper bits in its input register are not API inputs. Ordinary void adapter/wrapper results are excluded; typed flag/getter and GAP checked return words are compared.",
    "Callee-saved integer/FP registers, stack guards and interrupt masks are checked. Arbitrary aliases, private uninitialized memory, asynchronous concurrency, faults and physical timing are outside this replay.",
    "All831 other prior nongenerated objects and the GAP owner/table object remain identical. The observer and its two-byte flag storage are the only changed pre-existing allocated sections in this unit; added helpers/constants/gateways are separate new sections.",
    "R1 sources-check passes; global sources-check retains the unrelated unlisted G2 resident_rom_thumb_set.S failure. Final firmware linking, runtime placement and device boot remain unverified. Byte identity and a paid compiler are not requirements."
  ],
